   "id": "2-conformal-mapping-engine-plane-to-plane",
   "title": "2. Conformal Mapping Engine: s-Plane to z-Plane",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "The continuous-time complex frequency $s = \\sigma + j\\omega$ maps to the discrete-time complex frequency $z = r e^{j\\Omega}$ through the standard impulse-invariant conformal mapping:"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "z = e^{s T_s} = e^{(\\sigma + j\\omega) T_s} = e^{\\sigma T_s} \\cdot e^{j \\omega T_s}"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Matching polar form $z = r e^{j\\Omega}$:"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "r = \\vert z\\vert = e^{\\sigma T_s}, \\qquad \\Omega = \\omega T_s"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "2.1 The Three Geometric Invariants"
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "start": 1,
     "items": [
      "**Open Left-Half Plane (OLHP: $\\sigma < 0$):**"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\sigma < 0 \\implies e^{\\sigma T_s} < 1 \\implies \\vert z\\vert < 1 \\quad \\text{(Interior of the Unit Circle)}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "start": 2,
     "items": [
      "**Imaginary Axis ($j\\omega$-axis: $\\sigma = 0$):**"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\sigma = 0 \\implies e^{0} = 1 \\implies \\vert z\\vert = 1 \\quad \\text{(The Unit Circle)}"
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "start": 3,
     "items": [
      "**Open Right-Half Plane (ORHP: $\\sigma > 0$):**"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "\\sigma > 0 \\implies e^{\\sigma T_s} > 1 \\implies \\vert z\\vert > 1 \\quad \\text{(Exterior of the Unit Circle)}"
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "2.2 Discrete Frequency Landmarks on the Unit Circle"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Since $\\Omega = \\omega T_s$, the continuous frequency range maps periodically to the unit circle:"
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "$\\Omega = 0 \\implies z = e^{j 0} = +1$ (DC / Zero Frequency).",
      "$\\Omega = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\implies z = e^{j \\pi/2} = +j$ (Quarter Nyquist, $f_s / 4$).",
      "$\\Omega = \\pi \\implies z = e^{j \\pi} = -1$ (Half Nyquist, $f_s / 2$, Highest Discrete Frequency).",
      "$\\Omega = -\\pi \\implies z = e^{-j \\pi} = -1$ (Identical point to $+\\pi$ via branch wrap).",
      "$\\Omega = 2\\pi k \\implies z = e^{j 2\\pi k} = +1$ (Periodic wrap-around)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "**GATE Aliasing Insight:** The mapping $z = e^{s T_s}$ is **many-to-one**. Every horizontal strip of width $\\omega_s = \\frac{2\\pi}{T_s}$ in the $s$-plane wraps completely onto the entire $z$-plane. This cyclic periodicity is the origin of the $2\\pi$-periodicity of discrete-time spectra: $X(e^{j(\\Omega + 2\\pi)}) = X(e^{j\\Omega})$."
    }
   ]
